+HTTP/3 uses the pinned quic-go transport and the same request/response policy
+hooks. `fluxy-inspect` accepts routed QUIC packet flows from TUN and SOCKS5 UDP.
+Before interception, a `quic` IPC message asks the controller for an SSL policy
+decision (`quic-result` with `inspect` and `route`). Excluded hosts stay encrypted.
+The optional `packet_egress` service setting names the core outbound for native
+H3 and encrypted UDP egress; the Helper sets it to `direct`, which can itself use
+the chosen interface or SOCKS proxy. Requests preserve the original UDP endpoint
+unless a rule selects a different HTTP authority. HTTP/3 metadata uses `3.0`.
